  "oneLiner": "A turn-based Java dungeon engine separating board interactions, character abilities and enemy behavior.",
  "summary": "A command-line dungeon assignment models movement, combat and progression through an object hierarchy. Four character classes use different ability resources, while monsters, bosses and traps react on game ticks. Visitor-style dispatch connects an attempted move with the behavior of the tile it reaches.",
  "stack": [
    "Java",
    "Object-oriented design",
    "Visitor-style dispatch",
    "Command-line interface",
    "JUnit 5 test source"
  ],
  "capabilityGroups": [
    {
      "title": "One move, different outcomes",
      "summary": "Moving into empty ground swaps tile positions; a wall blocks movement; reaching an opposing unit starts combat. Dispatch separates these outcomes from the directional movement commands.",
      "details": [
        "The board stores a tile grid and synchronizes positions during swaps.",
        "The manager processes player input, enemy ticks and player resource updates."
      ],
