      "title": "Different threats on the same board",
      "summary": "Monsters chase within vision range and otherwise choose random moves. Bosses add timed special attacks, while traps cycle between visible and concealed glyphs and attack nearby players.",
      "details": [
        "Chasing uses a simple dominant-axis choice, not a general pathfinding algorithm.",
        "Defeating the remaining enemies loads the next level from an external map directory."
      ],
